meta {
  name: Lookup Campaign Mailer (Other Agency)
  type: http
  seq: 17
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/mailers/9c41b2d7ee01
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{onboardOwnerAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    // The campaign was committed with `assignment.mode: "all"`, which stores an
    // explicit `visibleAgencyIds: null` — every agency, including this one,
    // onboarded *after* the run.
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("says the mailer is taken, and nothing else", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.alreadyLogged).to.equal(true);
    // The load-bearing half. The lead belongs to another tenant, so its id is
    // withheld — the drawer renders "Already logged." with the action disabled
    // and names neither the agency nor the producer.
    expect(body.linkedLeadId).to.equal(null);
  });

  test("names no other tenant", function () {
    const serialized = JSON.stringify(res.getBody());
    expect(serialized).to.not.contain("demo-agency");
    expect(res.getBody()).to.not.have.property("visibleAgencyIds");
    expect(res.getBody()).to.not.have.property("campaignId");
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /mailers/:controlNumber — the same mailer, seen by a second agency

  Half of PAC-71's cross-agency contract, and the half that is about
  *non-disclosure* rather than refusal.

  - **Module:** `mailers`
  - **Permission:** `mailers:read`
  - **Data scope:** none — visibility is decided by the mailer's campaign.

  Sent as the owner of the agency **Platform Agencies › Onboard Agency** created
  minutes earlier in this run, which is why that request enables the `mailers`
  module: an agency that cannot reach the module would 403 here and prove
  nothing about visibility.

  ## Why this agency can see it at all

  `Commit Campaign (Append)` ran with `assignment.mode: "all"`, and the import
  stores that as an explicit `visibleAgencyIds: null`. The lookup then matches
  on `{ $or: [{ visibleAgencyIds: { $type: 'null' } }, { visibleAgencyIds:
  <caller> }] }` — `$type: 'null'`, never a bare `null`, which would also match a
  *missing* field and make every un-migrated mailer visible to every tenant.

  This is also the "including agencies onboarded later" case from the ticket,
  literally: the agency did not exist when the campaign was designed and does
  not appear in any stored list.

  ## Response `200`

  The full mailer view, with `alreadyLogged: true` and `linkedLeadId: null`.
  Those two fields answer different questions on purpose: `alreadyLogged` is
  **platform-wide**, because one lead per mailer is a platform rule;
  `linkedLeadId` is clamped to the caller's own scope, because a lead id from
  another tenant is that tenant's data. Together they say "taken, and not by
  you" without saying by whom.

  ## Errors
  - `403` — the caller's agency has the `mailers` module disabled.
  - `404` — the mailer exists but the caller's agency is not in
    `visibleAgencyIds`. Indistinguishable from "no such mailer", deliberately.
}
